8. Waterfall Model
Definition: Waterfall is a linear software development model in which each phase is completed before the next phase begins.

Roman Urdu: Is model mein pehle ek stage complete hota hai, phir next stage start hota hai.

Example: Pehle requirements, phir design, phir coding, phir testing.
9. Prototype Model
Definition: Prototype Model creates an initial working model of software to understand user requirements.

Example: Client ko final banking app banane se pehle demo design dikhana.

When used?
- When requirements are unclear.
- When client is unsure about the system.
Risk: Client prototype ko final product samajh sakta hai.
10. Spiral Model
Definition: Spiral Model combines iterative development with systematic risk analysis.

Roman Urdu: Is model mein software multiple cycles mein develop hota hai aur har cycle mein risks analyze kiye jate hain.

Example: Large banking system jahan security risks important hain.
11. Agile Model
Definition: Agile is an iterative software development model that supports continuous feedback and changing requirements.

Example: Food delivery app ko multiple small versions mein develop karna.
12. Plan-Driven Model
Definition: A plan-driven model follows predefined plans and requirements throughout software development.

Example: Government project jahan requirements aur documentation pehle se defined hon.
Agile	Plan-Driven
Flexible approach.	Planned approach.
Supports changing requirements.	Follows predefined requirements.
Frequent feedback.	More formal planning and documentation.
